\title{pathwaydepth: Depth Features for Spatial Pathway Graphs}
\description{
Converts the edge weights of a small weighted graph into edge-level depth features under two reference frames: the distribution of the same edge across a reference cohort (population-referenced depth) and the distribution of all edges within the same graph (within-sample depth). The depth is the univariate halfspace (Tukey) depth scaled to the unit interval, stabilised by subsampling the reference set. The package also provides the graph completion step, patient-level data splitting, a random forest classifier tuned on out-of-bag predictions, and the evaluation tools used to compare lung adenocarcinoma with lung squamous cell carcinoma on spatial pathway graphs derived from The Cancer Genome Atlas histology slides. The lung graphs are not included, because the licence of the data they are derived from does not allow derivatives to be distributed; simulated graphs are provided for examples.
}
